.TH ZSTREAM 8 "Nov 2, 2026"
.SH NAME
zstream \- manipulate zfs send streams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.LP
.nf
\fBzstream\fR dump [\fB-Cvd\fR] [\fIfile\fR]
\fBzstream\fR decompress [\fB-v\fR] [\fIobject\fR,\fIoffset\fR[,\fItype\fR]] ...
\fBzstream\fR drop_records [\fB-v\fR] [\fIobject\fR,\fIoffset\fR] ... [\fIfile\fR]
\fBzstream\fR recompress [\fB-v\fR] \fItype\fR [\fIfile\fR]
\fBzstream\fR token \fIresume_token\fR
\fBzstream\fR redup [\fB-v\fR] \fIfile\fR
\fBzstream\fR dedup [\fB-v\fR] [\fB-m\fR \fIpercent\fR] [\fB-c\fR \fIcache_dir\fR] [\fIfile\fR]
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
.LP
The \fBzstream\fR utility operates on send streams produced by the
\fBzfs send\fR command. See \fBzfs\fR(8). Each operation is invoked as a
subcommand, described below.
.sp
This is a separate binary from \fBzstreamdump\fR(8), which remains
available unchanged for existing scripts and tooling. \fBzstream dump\fR
provides equivalent functionality along with the additional stream
manipulation subcommands below.

.SS "zstream dump"
.LP
.nf
\fBzstream\fR dump [\fB-Cvd\fR] [\fIfile\fR]
.fi
.sp
Prints information about the specified send stream, including record
headers and counts. The stream is read from \fIfile\fR if given, or from
standard input.
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fB-C\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 4n
Suppress validation of checksums.
.RE
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fB-v\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 4n
Verbose. Print metadata for every record, not only \fBBEGIN\fR and
\fBEND\fR records.
.RE
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fB-d\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 4n
Dump the data contained in each record. Implies \fB-v\fR.
.RE

.SS "zstream decompress"
.LP
.nf
\fBzstream\fR decompress [\fB-v\fR] [\fIobject\fR,\fIoffset\fR[,\fItype\fR]] ...
.fi
.sp
Reads a send stream on standard input and decompresses selected records,
for use when the compression type recorded in a record's metadata is
incorrect. Each argument names the object number and byte offset of a
record to repair; every record for that object beginning at that offset
is decompressed, where possible. A record may not be repairable if it is
corrupted in some, but not all, of the stream's snapshots.
.sp
\fItype\fR is one of \fBoff\fR, \fBgzip\fR, \fBlz4\fR, \fBlzjb\fR, or
\fBzle\fR, and defaults to \fBlz4\fR if omitted. A type of
\fBoff\fR corrects the stream's metadata to indicate the record is
already uncompressed, without attempting decompression.
.sp
Note: \fBzstd\fR is not supported on this platform and is not accepted
as a \fItype\fR.
.sp
The repaired stream is written to standard output.
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fB-v\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 4n
Verbose. Print a summary of the records that were decompressed.
.RE

.SS "zstream drop_records"
.LP
.nf
\fBzstream\fR drop_records [\fB-v\fR] [\fIobject\fR,\fIoffset\fR] ... [\fIfile\fR]
.fi
.sp
Reads a send stream from \fIfile\fR, or from standard input, and drops
selected records, identified by object number and byte offset. Only
\fBWRITE\fR and \fBWRITE_EMBEDDED\fR records may currently be dropped.
Deduplicated streams are not supported. The repaired stream, with its
checksums regenerated, is written to standard output.
.sp
\fBdrop_record\fR is accepted as an alias for compatibility.
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fB-v\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 4n
Verbose. Print a summary of the records that were dropped.
.RE

.SS "zstream recompress"
.LP
.nf
\fBzstream\fR recompress [\fB-v\fR] \fItype\fR [\fIfile\fR]
.fi
.sp
Reads a send stream from \fIfile\fR, or from standard input, and writes
it to standard output with every \fBWRITE\fR record recompressed using
\fItype\fR, which is one of \fBoff\fR, \fBlzjb\fR, \fBgzip\fR,
\fBgzip-\fR\fIN\fR (\fIN\fR from 1 to 9), \fBzle\fR, or \fBlz4\fR.
Records that do not compress usefully are left uncompressed. Encrypted
(raw) records are passed through unchanged. Compression and
decompression run in parallel.
.sp
Note: \fBzstd\fR is not supported on this platform.
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fB-v\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 4n
Verbose.
.RE

.SS "zstream token"
.LP
.nf
\fBzstream\fR token \fIresume_token\fR
.fi
.sp
Decodes and prints the contents of a \fBzfs\fR resume token.

.SS "zstream redup"
.LP
.nf
\fBzstream\fR redup [\fB-v\fR] \fIfile\fR
.fi
.sp
\fBzfs send -D\fR can produce a deduplicated send stream, in which
duplicate blocks are referenced rather than retransmitted; support for
\fBzfs receive\fR of such streams is deprecated. \fBzstream redup\fR
reads a deduplicated stream from \fIfile\fR and writes an equivalent
non-deduplicated stream to standard output, allowing it to still be
received:
.sp
.RS 4n
.nf
# zstream redup \fIfile\fR | zfs receive ...
.fi
.RE
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fB-v\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 4n
Verbose. Print a summary of the records that were converted.
.RE

.SS "zstream dedup"
.LP
.nf
\fBzstream\fR dedup [\fB-v\fR] [\fB-m\fR \fIpercent\fR] [\fB-c\fR \fIcache_dir\fR] [\fIfile\fR]
.fi
.sp
The inverse of \fBzstream redup\fR. Reads a send stream from \fIfile\fR,
or from standard input, and writes a deduplicated stream to standard
output, replacing each \fBWRITE\fR record whose contents duplicate an
earlier one with a \fBWRITE_BYREF\fR record. Candidates are found by a
payload hash and confirmed by a full comparison of the records. The
dedup table is kept in memory and moves to disk if it outgrows its
memory budget.
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fB-v\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 4n
Verbose. Print periodic status updates.
.RE
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fB-m\fR \fIpercent\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 4n
The percentage of physical memory the dedup table may use before it
moves to disk. The default is 30.
.RE
.sp
.ne 2
.na
\fB\fB-c\fR \fIcache_dir\fR\fR
.ad
.RS 4n
The directory to hold the dedup table if it moves to disk. The default
is \fB/tmp\fR.
.RE

.SH ATTRIBUTES
.sp
.LP
See \fBattributes\fR(7) for descriptions of the following attributes:
.sp
.TS
box;
c | c
l | l .
ATTRIBUTE TYPE	ATTRIBUTE VALUE
_
Interface Stability	Uncommitted
.TE

